{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779034342,"nonce":"9lwfJSg9ga7QoU0HOYSO1EJTXls=","message":"### Chat grouping pressure from encoded Claude project paths\nThe current chat sidebar still exposes encoded source-path names for some Claude conversations, e.g. project buckets shaped like `-USERS-MLL-MAIN-...`. Issue 67a12d9 will add only a conservative UI fallback so these do not dominate the visible chat sidebar.\n\nThe durable fix belongs here: Mandible should own a central project registry that maps canonical project names to one or more normalized paths/worktrees/source identifiers, then all conversation ingestors (Claude logs, Codex logs, Gemini, SDK sessions, PTY sessions) should resolve project identity through that registry. The registry should also support user aliases/renames so a project can be displayed as `Mandible` or `Feedbax` regardless of which source log format produced the session.\n\nThis needs to be backend-owned rather than just a string-cleaning helper in the UI, because graph links, issue/session association, auth context, and future desktop project folders all need the same canonical identity.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}